26

The Chapter on Evil.

Make haste toward the good; restrain the mind from evil.
For when one is slow in doing good, the mind delights in evil.

If a person does evil, let him not do it again and again;
Let him not find pleasure in it, for the accumulation of evil is suffering.

If a person does good, let him do it again and again;
Let him find pleasure in it, for the accumulation of merit is happiness.

Even an evildoer sees good so long as his evil has not ripened;
But when his evil ripens, then the evildoer sees evil.

Even a good person sees evil so long as his good has not ripened;
But when his good ripens, then the good person sees good things.

Do not think lightly of evil, saying, "It will not come to me";
As a water jar is filled by the falling of drops,
So the fool fills himself with evil, little by little.
Do not think lightly of merit, saying, "It will not come to me";
As a water jar is filled by the falling of drops,
So the wise one fills himself with merit, little by little.

Like a merchant with little escort and much wealth avoiding a dangerous road,
Like one who loves life avoiding poison,
So should one avoid evil deeds.

If there is no wound on the hand, one may carry poison in it;
Poison does not harm one without a wound;
There is no evil for one who does no evil.

Whoever harms a harmless person,
